{
  "fps": 60,
  "label": "IBN AL-QAYYIM",
  "tagPrefix": "STORIES",
  "cadence": 3,
  "reels": [
    {
      "id": "01-doorstep",
      "hook": "A story Ibn al-Qayyim told about mercy",
      "cards": [
        {"text": "A man was walking down a quiet *street.*", "shape": "spark"},
        {"text": "A door flew open. A child ran *out,*", "shape": "door"},
        {"text": "crying, pushed out by his *mother.*", "shape": "doorOut"},
        {"text": "He walked away, then *stopped.*", "shape": "road"},
        {"text": "There was nowhere else to *go.*", "shape": "scatter"},
        {"text": "He came back. The door was *shut.*", "shape": "doorShut"},
        {"text": "", "pills": ["Pushed out", "Nowhere to go", "Came back"]},
        {"text": "He laid his cheek on the doorstep and *slept.*", "shape": "threshold"},
        {"text": "She ran out and held him: *“Who else would shelter you?”*", "shape": "heart", "flare": true},
        {"text": "And Allah is more merciful than any *mother.*", "shape": "ring"}
      ],
      "book": {"ar": "مدارج السالكين", "en": "Madarij al-Salikin", "sub": "TOLD BY IBN AL-QAYYIM"}
    },
    {
      "id": "02-garden",
      "hook": "What his teacher said from a prison cell",
      "cards": [
        {"text": "Damascus. His teacher was in *prison.*", "shape": "spark"},
        {"text": "Ibn Taymiyyah, locked in the *Citadel.*", "shape": "bars"},
        {"text": "He said: what can my enemies do to *me?*", "shape": "ring"},
        {"text": "My paradise and my garden are in my *chest.*", "shape": "tree"},
        {"text": "Wherever I go, it stays with *me.*", "shape": "orbit"},
        {"text": "", "pills": ["Prison: solitude", "Killing: martyrdom", "Exile: a journey"]},
        {"text": "When fear gripped us, we went to *him.*", "shape": "wave"},
        {"text": "One look, a few words, and it all *lifted.*", "shape": "sun", "flare": true},
        {"text": "Into openness, strength and *certainty.*", "shape": "star8"}
      ],
      "book": {"ar": "الوابل الصيب", "en": "Al-Wabil al-Sayyib", "sub": "IBN AL-QAYYIM ON HIS TEACHER"}
    },
    {
      "id": "03-breakfast",
      "hook": "The morning routine of Ibn Taymiyyah",
      "cards": [
        {"text": "Ibn al-Qayyim watched his teacher one *morning.*", "shape": "spark"},
        {"text": "He prayed *Fajr.*", "shape": "dawn"},
        {"text": "Then he sat, remembering *Allah.*", "shape": "ring"},
        {"text": "Hour after *hour,*", "shape": "spiral"},
        {"text": "until it was nearly *midday.*", "shape": "arcs"},
        {"text": "", "pills": ["Fajr", "Dhikr", "Midday"]},
        {"text": "Then he turned to his student and *said:*", "shape": "orbit"},
        {"text": "“This is my *breakfast.*”", "shape": "sun", "flare": true},
        {"text": "“Without it, my strength would *collapse.*”", "shape": "line"}
      ],
      "book": {"ar": "الوابل الصيب", "en": "Al-Wabil al-Sayyib", "sub": "IBN AL-QAYYIM ON HIS TEACHER"}
    },
    {
      "id": "04-citadel",
      "hook": "Prison couldn't stop Ibn al-Qayyim",
      "cards": [
        {"text": "He was jailed in the Citadel of *Damascus,*", "shape": "spark"},
        {"text": "kept apart from his *teacher.*", "shape": "bars"},
        {"text": "So he turned to the *Quran.*", "shape": "book"},
        {"text": "Reciting slowly. Reflecting on every *verse.*", "shape": "wave"},
        {"text": "And Allah opened great good to *him.*", "shape": "star8", "flare": true},
        {"text": "", "pills": ["Prison", "Quran", "Opening"]},
        {"text": "He was freed only after his teacher *died.*", "shape": "line"},
        {"text": "His student Ibn Rajab recorded it *all.*", "shape": "arch"}
      ],
      "book": {"ar": "ذيل طبقات الحنابلة", "en": "Dhayl Tabaqat al-Hanabila", "sub": "IBN RAJAB, HIS STUDENT"}
    },
    {
      "id": "05-road",
      "hook": "He wrote a classic while travelling",
      "cards": [
        {"text": "Zad al-Ma'ad: the Prophet's ﷺ *guidance.*", "shape": "spark"},
        {"text": "He wrote it on a *journey.*", "shape": "road"},
        {"text": "Not at home. Not *settled.*", "shape": "wave"},
        {"text": "“My heart had a branch in every *valley.*”", "shape": "scatter"},
        {"text": "Yet it covers prayer, trade, medicine and *more.*", "shape": "book"},
        {"text": "", "pills": ["Travel", "A scattered heart", "Zad al-Ma'ad"]},
        {"text": "Read and taught for nearly seven *centuries.*", "shape": "arcs", "flare": true},
        {"text": "Its title: provision for the *Hereafter.*", "shape": "star8"}
      ],
      "book": {"ar": "زاد المعاد", "en": "Zad al-Ma'ad", "sub": "FROM HIS INTRODUCTION"}
    },
    {
      "id": "06-prayer",
      "hook": "What Ibn Kathir saw in his friend",
      "cards": [
        {"text": "Ibn Kathir knew him *well.*", "shape": "spark"},
        {"text": "“I was among the closest people to *him.*”", "shape": "halves"},
        {"text": "“I know no one in our time who worshipped *more.*”", "shape": "arch"},
        {"text": "He made his prayer very *long.*", "shape": "line"},
        {"text": "Long bowing. Long *prostration.*", "shape": "arcs"},
        {"text": "", "pills": ["Bowing", "Prostration", "Never rushed"]},
        {"text": "His companions sometimes blamed him for *it.*", "shape": "scatter"},
        {"text": "He never *stopped.*", "shape": "ring", "flare": true}
      ],
      "book": {"ar": "البداية والنهاية", "en": "Al-Bidaya wa'n-Nihaya", "sub": "IBN KATHIR, HIS FRIEND"}
    },
    {
      "id": "07-books",
      "hook": "He collected books like no one else",
      "cards": [
        {"text": "He loved one thing *deeply:* books.", "shape": "spark"},
        {"text": "Works of the early and later *scholars.*", "shape": "stack"},
        {"text": "Others couldn't gather a *tenth* of them.", "shape": "bars"},
        {"text": "He passed away in 751 *AH.*", "shape": "line"},
        {"text": "His sons sold his books for a long *time,*", "shape": "scatter"},
        {"text": "", "pills": ["Collected", "Read", "Wrote"]},
        {"text": "besides the ones they kept for *themselves.*", "shape": "book"},
        {"text": "Knowledge outlives the one who carries *it.*", "shape": "star8", "flare": true}
      ],
      "book": {"ar": "الدرر الكامنة", "en": "Al-Durar al-Kamina", "sub": "IBN HAJAR · IBN KATHIR"}
    },
    {
      "id": "08-makkah",
      "hook": "The people of Makkah were amazed by him",
      "cards": [
        {"text": "He performed Hajj many *times.*", "shape": "spark"},
        {"text": "He stayed on in *Makkah.*", "shape": "cube"},
        {"text": "Its people spoke of his *tawaf,*", "shape": "cubeOrbit"},
        {"text": "circling again and *again,*", "shape": "spiral"},
        {"text": "and of how hard he *worshipped.*", "shape": "arch"},
        {"text": "", "pills": ["Hajj", "Tawaf", "Worship"]},
        {"text": "Even Makkah's people found it *amazing.*", "shape": "sun", "flare": true},
        {"text": "Ibn Rajab sat in his classes in his final *year.*", "shape": "book"}
      ],
      "book": {"ar": "ذيل طبقات الحنابلة", "en": "Dhayl Tabaqat al-Hanabila", "sub": "IBN RAJAB, HIS STUDENT"}
    },
    {
      "id": "09-nothing",
      "hook": "The humility of Ibn Taymiyyah",
      "cards": [
        {"text": "Ibn al-Qayyim often heard his teacher *say:*", "shape": "spark"},
        {"text": "“I own *nothing.*”", "shape": "ring"},
        {"text": "“Nothing comes from *me.*”", "shape": "line"},
        {"text": "“And there is nothing in *me.*”", "shape": "scatter"},
        {"text": "When people praised him to his *face,*", "shape": "halves"},
        {"text": "", "pills": ["Nothing mine", "Nothing from me", "Nothing in me"]},
        {"text": "he said: “By Allah, I renew my Islam every *moment.*”", "shape": "star8", "flare": true},
        {"text": "“I have not yet become a Muslim *properly.*”", "shape": "wave"}
      ],
      "book": {"ar": "مدارج السالكين", "en": "Madarij al-Salikin", "sub": "IBN AL-QAYYIM ON HIS TEACHER"}
    },
    {
      "id": "10-name",
      "hook": "Why was he called Ibn Qayyim al-Jawziyya?",
      "cards": [
        {"text": "Damascus, 691 *AH.*", "shape": "spark"},
        {"text": "His father looked after a school: *al-Jawziyya.*", "shape": "arch"},
        {"text": "Its caretaker was called its *qayyim.*", "shape": "book"},
        {"text": "So the son became *Ibn Qayyim al-Jawziyya.*", "shape": "orbit"},
        {"text": "In 712 AH he met Ibn *Taymiyyah.*", "shape": "halves"},
        {"text": "", "pills": ["691 · Born", "712 · His teacher", "751 · Returned to Allah"]},
        {"text": "Sixteen years at his teacher's *side.*", "shape": "arcs"},
        {"text": "Seven centuries on, we still read *him.*", "shape": "star8", "flare": true}
      ],
      "book": {"ar": "ذيل طبقات الحنابلة", "en": "Dhayl Tabaqat al-Hanabila", "sub": "IBN RAJAB · IBN KATHIR"}
    }
  ]
}
